Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user's single request (verbatim): "Create a single-file HTML page (/app/index.html) with all CSS and JavaScript inline and zero external assets. Never use image generation tools or models. Draw the scene with code (HTML, CSS, SVG, canvas or WebGL); embedded raster artwork is disallowed. Render a dark, atmospheric hero scene featuring a single, steaming bowl of vegan ramen as the sole visual focus. Make the dish feel alive and appetizing — with natural motion, ambient warmth, and interactive response to the mouse. Keep the scene pure (no UI, text, or menus), responsive on all screens, and respectful of prefers-reduced-motion."

   Hard constraints to keep honoring: single file at `/app/index.html`; all CSS/JS inline; zero external assets; never use image generation tools/models; no embedded raster artwork (everything drawn by code at runtime); no UI/text/menus in the scene; responsive; respects `prefers-reduced-motion`. System reminders also ask me to keep the user updated with brief progress notes while working. (/app is not a git repo; no commits requested.)

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Pure Canvas 2D rendering (deliberately no WebGL: headless Chrome's software-WebGL fallback is deprecated, so Canvas 2D gives identical results everywhere)
   - "Bowl units" coordinate system: 1 unit = outer rim radius; `view.K` = device px per unit; origin `(view.ox, view.oy)` = rim centre; orthographic 3/4 camera with `SQ=0.6` (sin elevation), `CQ=0.8`; projection `P(x,z,y) = [x, YB + z*SQ − y*CQ]`
   - Static layers painted once per size into offscreen canvases (background/table, bowl+broth+submerged noodles+lip, one sprite per topping, chopsticks); dynamic layers composed per frame
   - Bowl shaded as a surface of revolution: stacked half-ellipse strokes with per-slice linear gradients computed from a lighting function in linear light (`lin()` converts to sRGB)
   - CPU stable-fluids steam simulation (semi-Lagrangian advection, SOR Gauss-Seidel pressure projection with open boundaries, buoyancy, vorticity confinement, wandering eddies, random gusts, dye diffusion, height-dependent decay), velocity grid ~88×73, dye grid 2× that, rendered to ImageData and upscaled with bilinear `drawImage`
   - Pointer = warm lantern: light position eases to pointer; drives broth sheen, lip highlight arcs, exterior highlight, table spill (`color-dodge`), bowl shadow, `overlay` food light, steam brightness, per-glint specular flashes, pointer glow; pointer motion stirs steam and trails ripples on broth; click = big ripple + steam puff (or gust of air off-broth)
   - Floaters on broth (oil droplets, sesame, scallion rings, chili flakes) advected by a divergence-free convection field, repelled by topping footprints (`obstacles`), pushed by ripples/pointer
   - Glint system: painters register facets via `glint(g,x,y,s)`; `makeSprite` collects them with random normals; `drawGlints` flashes them when light/half-vector aligns
   - Reduced motion: no rAF loop, one composed static frame (steam pre-warmed), only the light eases briefly on pointer move (`easeStill`)
   - Adaptive quality: coarser steam grid if the sim is slow, DPR reduction only when frames are very slow; pre-warm benchmark picks coarse steam from first frame on slow machines
   - Deterministic seeded PRNG (`rng`, mulberry32) and value noise/fbm so the dish is plated identically each load
   - Dev workflow: source parts concatenated by a build script; puppeteer-core + headless Chromium for screenshots, real mouse input, reduced-motion emulation, profiling

3. Files and Code Sections:

   **IMPORTANT WORKFLOW:** Never edit `/app/index.html` directly. Edit parts in `<TMP>/dev/src/` then run `<TMP>/dev/build.sh`, which concatenates `00_head.html` + all `*.js` (sorted) + `99_tail.html` into `/app/index.html`, also writes a debug twin `<TMP>/shots/debug.html` (inserting `<TMP>/dev/debug/80_debug.js` just before `98_close.js`), and syntax-checks the script. Last build: "syntax ok, bytes 106287".

